---
title: Matcha Amaretti Cookies
image: https://frommybowl.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Matcha_Crinkle_Cookies_Vegan_FromMyBowl-16-768x1152.jpg
author: Jesse Szewczyk
---

Preheat the oven to 325*F and line 2 #baking sheets{} with parchment paper.

In a #large bowl{}, combine @almond flour{2.5%cups}, @matcha{2%tbsp}, @salt{1/4%tsp}, and @sugar{1%cup}. Whisk until matcha is evenly distributed.

> Split the matcha 3:1 between sweet and bitter matcha, simply due to it being what I had on hand. If doing straight matcha or bitter matcha you may need/want less. The original recipe called for half, but the sweet matcha is less flavorful, so the extra amount helps.

In the bowl of a #stand mixer{} with the whisk attachment, add @egg whites{3}(room temperature), @vanilla extract{2%tsp}, and @almond extract{1%tsp}.

Mix on medium speed until slightly frothy, ~{2-3%minutes}.

Increase speed to high and whip until doubled in volume and stiff peaks form, about ~{1-2%minutes} more.

Transfer the whipped eggs to the bowl with the dry ingredients and mix until a thick dough forms.

Add @sugar{1/4%cup} to a plate or shallow bowl. Add @confectioner's sugar{1/2%cup} to another plate/bowl.

> We halved the coatings because we found the original amount created a lot of waste. YMMV.

Portion out dough into 1 inch spheres. Roll each sphere through the granulated sugar first, then the confectioner's sugar, shaking off any excess of the confectioner's sugar before adding to the baking sheets, placing each about 3 inches apart.

Using the bottom of a cup or glass, or the palm of your hand, gently press down the tops of the spheres so they are around 1/2 inch thick discs.

Bake both sheets at the same time, swapping the top and bottom halfway through. Bake until the cookies are cracked and just starting to brown on the bottoms, ~{23-26%minutes}.

Remove from the oven and let cool slightly before transferring to a wire rack.

> Cookies keep for up to a week in an airtight container.
